  "brief": {
    "prose": "The Lot: a four-hundred-metre square of studio back lot, flat and paved, with a raised loading dock behind the lobby building. Two neighborhoods stand on it — the OOC Area by the south gate and the Staff Lobby in the north-east — joined by the studio tour, a bus loop past the security gate and the water tower. It is the first content of every fresh world: where newcomers arrive, learn the commands, and meet the staff.",
    "origin": "Most of the cast's names and a few of their lines are an homage to a 2004 film about a high school (doc 06 §15): the quotations are short, nothing else is imported, and the setting is a film lot that never names it.",
    "answers": {
      "q.scale": "one lot, walkable end to end",
      "q.mood": "a working studio on a quiet day",
      "q.travel": "the tour bus, and feet"
    }
  },
